Navigate to your cloned GitHub project directory:
Bash
cd /path/to/your/cloned-repo
Review proxy.md and Update nginx.conf
View the contents of proxy.md to confirm the specific routing directives provided for your setup:

Bash
cat proxy.md

Open the provided nginx.conf file in a text editor:

Bash
nano nginx.conf

Locate the location /api/ (or location /) block. Update the proxy_pass directive with your Internal ALB DNS Name:

Nginx
location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://<YOUR-INTERNAL-ALB-DNS-NAME>/;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for

Replace the Default Nginx Configuration
Create a backup of your original default Nginx configuration file:

Bash
sudo mv /etc/nginx/nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf.bak


Copy your newly edited nginx.conf from your project folder to /etc/nginx/:

Bash
sudo cp nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf


Test and Restart Nginx1.Test Nginx Configuration Syntax:
Run the syntax check command to ensure there are no formatting errors:
  
Bash
sudo nginx -t

Restart Nginx Service:
Apply your updated configuration by restarting the Nginx daemon:
Bash
  sudo systemctl restart nginx

Verify Nginx Status 
  Bash
sudo systemctl status nginx

Verify Web Tier to Application Tier Communication
On your Web Tier EC2 instance, execute a curl test to verify local reverse proxy routing through Nginx:

Bash
curl -I http://localhost/api/
